# Reusable Components

Any component that is (or could be) used in more than one place MUST live in `components/`.

- Do NOT define reusable components inline inside `app/**/page.tsx` or other route files. Route files compose components; they do not define shared ones.
- One component per file. File name is kebab-case and matches the export (e.g. `wellness-place-card.tsx` → `WellnessPlaceCard`).
- Import via the `@/components/...` alias, never relative `../../components`.
- Type props with an explicit `interface <Name>Props`.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — reusable card defined inline in a route
export default function FeedPage() {
  const Card = ({ title }: { title: string }) => <div>{title}</div>;
  return <Card title="Meditation" />;
}

// ✅ GOOD — extracted to components/, imported by alias
import { WellnessPlaceCard } from "@/components/wellness-place-card";

export default function FeedPage() {
  return <WellnessPlaceCard title="Meditation" />;
}
```

If you find yourself duplicating JSX, stop and extract it into `components/` first.
